  "id": "COMPOUND:36014 - PROTEIN:3691",
  "verbalization": "Jasplakinolide Z1 is implicated in the pathway leading to Arginine deiminase through multiple indirect mechanisms. The drug is shown to target Isoleucine--tRNA ligase, which in turn is targeted by a compound with a complex chemical structure, ultimately leading to the activation of Arginine deiminase. Similarly, Jasplakinolide Z1 is also linked to CEM-SS, which is targeted by another compound, and both of these are ultimately linked to Arginine deiminase. This suggests that Jasplakinolide Z1 may exert its effects through a series of molecular interactions that ultimately converge on Arginine deiminase. The evidence supports a pathway where Jasplakinolide Z1 acts as a modulator of downstream targets, potentially influencing the activity of Arginine deiminase through a chain of enzymatic or biochemical interactions. The integration of these pathways highlights the complexity of the molecular interactions involved, with Jasplakinolide Z1 possibly playing a role in the regulation of Arginine deiminase through a series of intermediate targets.",
